                <pb facs="0946" n="836" sameAs="frus:frus1931v03/pg836"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.003/654: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-05-04T14:00:00+08:00">May 4, 1931—2 p.m.</date><lb/>[Received
                        May 4—8:50 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>British Minister informs me that in discussions regarding personal status matters
                    he is having trouble getting Chinese to accept certain amendments suggested by
                    British Foreign Office. Chinese say proposals put forward by us are much easier
                    for them to accept. Please telegraph text of our article on this subject that I
                    may show it to British Minister.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
